  "recommended_action": "Handle T-2 first (ROE-4.6). It heads for the fuel farm with about 2.4 min to run. Rung 1: keep the gimbal on T-2 and keep the PVID. Rung 2 now (operator approval): warn, alert base security, and notify the control room. The pilot is unknown, so follow ROE-6.5. Rung 2 alone is unlikely to work in the time left. Rung 3: the operator asks the control room to approve the RF jammer on T-2. The link is live. Before approving, the control room must confirm that no crewed aircraft is within 3 km and no lane vessel is within 2 km (ROE-5.2). I have no data on either. The lane is 2057 m from T-2 by geometry, which is a thin margin. Plan for link loss (ROE-5.3). The drone may continue on its own toward the fuel farm, or land or fall with its payload. The target is over water now, which is the safest place to act, so decide quickly. Have the interceptor (rung 4) ready as the next step if the jam fails or T-2 stays on course. Rung 4 needs control-room approval. Keep T-1 at rung 0-1. It has valid Remote ID, a pilot at the marina and a regatta match, but it is not a listed friendly drone (ROE-2.6). Keep tracking it and watch the altitude disagreement. Optionally have security speak to its pilot at the marina (ROE-6.1)."
